# An uppercase sigil does not interpolate, and that changes both stops.
#
# `#{` is content here - the C only returns at a `#` when the row says the
# family interpolates - so the first body is the whole `no #{x} seam`. The
# backslash flips the other way: without interpolation it stops the body only
# when the *next* byte is the closing delimiter, which is exactly the escape
# in the second line and is not the two backslashes in any other.
roots 1
mends 0
holds quoted_content
spans quoted_content 7 19
spans quoted_content 28 35
spans quoted_content 37 50
